 Here's a Dart function that computes the top three coins with the highest average profit and the top three coins with the highest average loss based on the given list of transaction objects:

```dart
import 'dart:collection';

class Transaction {
  final String coinName;
  final DateTime dateTime;
  final double profitLoss; // positive for profit, negative for loss

  Transaction(this.coinName, this.dateTime, this.profitLoss);
}

List<String> topCoinsWithHighestAverageProfitAndLoss(List<Transaction> transactions) {
  Map<String, double> profitMap = {};
  Map<String, double> lossMap = {};

  for (Transaction transaction in transactions) {
    if (transaction.profitLoss > 0) {
      profitMap[transaction.coinName] = (profitMap[transaction.coinName] ?? 0.0) + transaction.profitLoss;
    } else {
      lossMap[transaction.coinName] = (lossMap[transaction.coinName] ?? 0.0) + transaction.profitLoss;
    }
  }

  List<MapEntry<String, double>> profits = profitMap.entries.map((entry) => MapEntry(entry.key, entry.value / transactions.length)).toList();
  List<MapEntry<String, double>> losses = lossMap.entries.map((entry) => MapEntry(entry.key, entry.value / transactions.length)).toList();

  profits.sort((a, b) => b.value.compareTo(a.value));
  losses.sort((a, b) => a.value.compareTo(b.value));

  return [
    "Top 3 Coins with Highest Average Profit:",
    ...profits.take(3).map((entry) => entry.key),
    "",
    "Top 3 Coins with Highest Average Loss:",
    ...losses.take(3).map((entry) => entry.key),
  ].join("\n");
}
```

This function uses a map to store the total profit or loss for each coin, then calculates the average profit or loss for each coin and sorts them accordingly

