% Apply Sobel operator in y direction on the filtered image
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```
In this code, we first apply a Gaussian filter using the `imgaussfilt` function with a standard deviation of 2. Then, we apply the Sobel operator on the filtered image instead of the original grayscale image. This helps reduce the noise in the image before detecting the edges.

