 To retrieve the username from a JSON Web Token (JWT) in an ASP.NET C# WebApi project, follow these steps:

1. First, make sure that you have installed the `Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens` NuGet package. This package contains the necessary components for parsing and validating JWT tokens.

   Run this command in the terminal or Package Manager Console:
    ```
    Install-Package Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens
    ```

2. Create a method to extract the username from the JWT token. Here's an example of how you can implement it:

   ```csharp
   using System;
   using System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt;
   using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer;
   using Microsoft.Extensions.Claims;

   public static string GetUsernameFromJwtToken(string jwtToken)
   {
       try
       {
           var handler = new JwtSecurityTokenHandler();
           var jsonToken = handler.ReadJwtToken(jwtToken);
           return jsonToken.Claims.FirstOrDefault(x => x.Type == ClaimTypes.Name)?.Value;
       }
       catch (Exception ex)
       {
           throw new Exception("Invalid or expired token", ex);
       }
   }
   ```

3. Now you can use the method in your controller action to get the username from the JWT token. Here's an example:

